  "date": "October 2026",
  "abstract": "Covers the Common Expression Language (CEL) language definition published in the cel-expr/cel-spec repository (formerly google/cel-spec): syntax, values and gradual typing, operators and precedence, macros, standard functions, error and unknown semantics, and the performance model. It lists four version lines: CEL v0.25 (current, pinned to v0.25.3), CEL v0.24 and CEL v0.6 (legacy, upgraded from), and the unreleased master branch (preview, posture track). SKILL.md holds the invariants and workflow; references split out versions, syntax and types, operators, macros and functions, errors and evaluation, and writing safe expressions.",
